            <h3>Terminal Configuration:</h3>
            <p>MIA operates from a multi-terminal complex with distinct carrier assignments.</p>
            <h4>North Terminal (Concourse D)</h4>
            <p>Primarily American Airlines and oneworld partners.</p>
            <p><b>Contained within:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Extensive check-in hall with self-service kiosks and bag drop</li>
                <li>Admirals Club, Flagship Lounge, and Flagship First Dining for premium passengers</li>
                <li>Dining reflects Miami's Cuban, Colombian, and broader Latin American influences</li>
                <li>Duty-free shopping and retail concourse</li>
                <li>Direct access to Miami Central Station for ground transit connections</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Central Terminal (Concourses E, F, G)</h3>
            <p>Mixed carrier operations including Delta, international airlines, and charter services.</p>
            <h4>South Terminal (Concourses H, J)</h4>
            <p>Primarily international and long-haul carriers.</p>
            <p><b>Features:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>International departure gates with customs and immigration facilities</li>
                <li>Diverse airline lounges, including Air France and VIP lounges</li>
                <li>Expanded retail and dining options</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Reaching MIA:</h3>
            <h4>Metrorail and MIA Mover</h4>
            <p>The Orange Line connects downtown Miami to the airport via the MIA Mover automated people mover.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Most economical option at approximately $2.25</li>
                <li>Reliable service avoiding traffic congestion</li>
                <li>Connections tothe  broader Miami-Dade transit network</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Private Vehicles</h4>
            <p>Taxis, Uber, and Lyft serve all terminals.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Downtown Miami: $20-$35, 15-25 minutes</li>
                <li>Miami Beach: $35-$55, 30-45 minutes</li>
                <li>Fort Lauderdale: $60-$90, 45-60 minutes</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Parking Structure:</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Dolphin Garage: Adjacent to terminal; premium convenience; $17-$25 daily</li>
                <li>Flamingo Garage: Short walk or shuttle; moderate rates; $15-$20 daily</li>
                <li>Long-Term Parking: Remote with shuttle; $10-$15 daily; optimal for extended European trips</li>
                <li>Cell Phone Waiting Lot: Free short-term holding for arriving passenger pickup</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Lounge Access:</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>American Airlines Admirals Club - Multiple locations; membership or day pass access</li>
                <li>Flagship Lounge - Premium cabin and elite status passengers</li>
                <li>Air France Lounge - SkyTeam business and first class passengers</li>
                <li>Delta Sky Club - Delta premium passengers and members</li>
                <li>VIP Lounge Miami - Priority Pass and paid access</li>
            </ul>
            <h2>Arrival Airport: Paris Charles de Gaulle Airport (CDG)</h2>
            <p>Charles de Gaulle stands as France's aviation masterpiece - sprawling, complex, and endlessly fascinating in its architectural ambition.</p>
