            <h3>Terminal Architecture:</h3>
            <p>CDG's layout confounds first-time visitors but rewards those who study it.</p>
            <h4>Terminal 1</h4>
            <p>The iconic circular terminal designed by Paul Andreu resembles a giant octopus.</p>
            <p><b>Characteristics:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Central check-in and baggage claim core</li>
                <li>Satellite departure gates connected by underground passages</li>
                <li>Recently renovated with modern amenities</li>
                <li>Primarily serves Star Alliance carriers and some others</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Terminal 2</h4>
            <p>The largest and most complex, subdivided into multiple sub-terminals (2A through 2G).</p>
            <p><b>Key details:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>2E, 2F, 2G: Primarily Air France and SkyTeam partners; most Miami flights arrive here</li>
                <li>2A, 2B, 2C, 2D: Mix of oneworld, Star Alliance, and other carriers</li>
                <li>Automated CDGVAL shuttle connects Terminal 2 sub-sections</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Terminal 3</h4>
            <p>Dedicated to low-cost and charter carriers.</p>
            <h3>Immigration and Customs at CDG:</h3>
            <p>Passengers arriving from Miami clear French entry formalities.</p>
            <p><b>Required documentation:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Valid passport with at least three months' validity beyond planned departure</li>
                <li>No visa is required for US citizens staying under 90 days within the Schengen area</li>
                <li>Return or onward travel documentation</li>
                <li>Accommodation details, if requested by border officers</li>
            </ul>
            <p>US citizens enjoy visa-free entry for tourism, business, or family visits up to 90 days within any 180-day Schengen period.</p>
            <h3>Ground Transportation from CDG to Paris:</h3>
            <h4>RER B Commuter Rail</h4>
            <p>The most popular option, connecting directly to central Paris stations.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><B>Single ticket:</B> approximately €11.80</li>
                <li><B>Journey to Châtelet-Les Halles: </B>35-40 minutes</li>
                <li><B>Continues to Saint-Michel</B> Notre-Dame, Luxembourg, and Denfert-Rochereau</li>
                <li><B>Frequent departure</B>s every 10-15 minutes</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>RoissyBus</h4>
            <p>Direct bus service to the Opera Garnier.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><B>Flat fare:</B> approximately €14.20</li>
                <li><B>Journey time: </B>60-75 minutes depending on traffic</li>
                <li><B>Departures</B> every 15-30 minutes</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Taxi</h4>
            <p>Official taxis with illuminated roof signs operate from designated ranks.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><B>Fixed </B>airport supplement applies</li>
                <li><B>To Right Bank (north of Seine):</B> approximately €55-€62</li>
                <li><B>To Left Bank (south of Seine): </B>approximately €62-€70</li>
                <li><B>Always use official taxi ranks; </B>refuse unsolicited offers in the arrivals hall</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Private Transfer and Rideshare</h4>
            <p>Uber, Bolt, and pre-booked private transfers available.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Similar pricing to taxis but with app-based convenience</li>
                <li>Meet-and-greet services are available for a premium</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Le Bus Direct (formerly Les Cars Air France)</h4>
            <p>Airport coach service to key Paris locations.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><B>Line 2:</B> CDG to Porte Maillot, Étoile (Arc de Triomphe)</li>
                <li><B>Line 4: </B>CDG to Gare de Lyon, Gare Montparnasse</li>
                <li><B>Fares: </B>approximately €18-€24</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Alternative Airports</h3>
            <h4>Paris Orly Airport (ORY)</h4>
            <p>Paris's second airport, located closer to the city center.</p>
            <p><b>Strategic value:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Some transatlantic flights, particularly by French Bee and seasonal carriers</li>
                <li>Closer to the southern Paris suburbs and Versailles</li>
                <li>Smaller and less overwhelming than CDG</li>
                <li>OrlyBus connects to Denfert-Rochereau in 30 minutes</li>
            </ul>
            <p>No other viable alternatives exist for direct Paris access, though travelers might consider:</p>
            <h4>London Heathrow (LHR)</h4>
            <p>For UK-France combination trips.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Eurostar train connects London to Paris in 2 hours 15 minutes</li>
                <li>Multiple daily Miami-London frequencies</li>
                <li>Useful for multi-city European itineraries</li>
            </ul>
