            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>Q1: How long is the nonstop flight from Miami to Paris?</h3>
            <p>The nonstop journey spans approximately 8 hours 30 minutes to 9 hours 15 minutes, depending on aircraft type, winds, and routing. Eastbound flights typically run shorter than westbound returns due to prevailing jet stream assistance.</p>

            <h3>Q2: Which airlines fly nonstop between Miami and Paris?</h3>
            <p>Air France and American Airlines operate daily nonstop service. Air France offers multiple daily departures. Delta may operate seasonally during summer months. All flights arrive at Charles de Gaulle Airport.</p>

            <h3>Q3: Do US citizens need a visa for France?</h3>
            <p>No visas are required for tourism or business stays under 90 days within any 180-day Schengen period. A valid passport with at least three months' validity beyond departure suffices-no additional documentation needed for standard visits.</p>

            <h3>Q4: What is the cheapest month to fly from Miami to Paris?</h3>
            <p>November and January historically offer the lowest fares, with economy round-trips sometimes available below $450. August commands premium pricing. Tuesday and Wednesday departures consistently undercut weekend travel by significant margins.</p>

            <h3>Q5: How do I get from Charles de Gaulle Airport to central Paris?</h3>
            <p>RER B train reaches central Paris in 35-40 minutes for approximately €12. RoissyBus serves Opera in 60-75 minutes for €14. Taxis charge fixed rates of €55-€70 depending on the destination zone. All options depart frequently throughout the day.</p>

            <h3>Q6: Can I use US dollars in Paris?</h3>
            <p>The Euro is France's currency. US dollars are not accepted. Credit cards work universally; chip-and-PIN cards are preferred. ATMs plentiful throughout the city. Notify your bank before traveling to prevent card blocks.</p>

            <h3>Q7: What terminal do Miami flights arrive at in Paris?</h3>
            <p>Air France flights typically arrive at Terminal 2E or 2F. American flights usually arrive at Terminal 2A or 2B. Terminal 2 sub-sections connect via the automated CDGVAL shuttle. Allow extra time for terminal navigation.</p>

            <h3>Q8: Is Paris safe for American tourists?</h3>
            <p>Paris is generally safe with standard urban precautions. Pickpockets operate in tourist zones, on the Metro, and near major attractions. Violent crime against tourists is rare. Police presence is visible. The emergency number is 112 throughout Europe.</p>

            <h3>Q9: What should I pack for Paris?</h3>
            <p>Comfortable walking shoes essential for cobblestones and museum marathons. Smart casual attire for evening dining; Parisians dress well. Layers accommodate temperature swings. Universal power adapter for European outlets. Umbrella for unpredictable showers year-round.</p>

            <h3>Q10: How early should I arrive at Miami airport for Paris flights?</h3>
            <p>Arrive three hours before scheduled departure for international flights from Miami. Security queues vary unpredictably. Check-in closes 60 minutes before departure on most carriers. Allow additional time if checking bags or needing assistance.</p>











